WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.957 --> 00:00:15.832
Six weeks passed while we worked hard.

2
00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:20.965
We planted fruit trees at Falconhurst. After that we worked at Tentholm.

3
00:00:20.966 --> 00:00:23.964
I wanted to make it safe in case of emergency.

4
00:00:23.965 --> 00:00:28.509
First we planted a thick, prickly hedge that would protect us from wild animals.

5
00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:32.584
Then we mounted two cannons from the wreck on a hill above the bay.

6
00:00:32.585 --> 00:00:37.488
The boys were growing strong as I encouraged them to run, climb, and swim.

7
00:00:37.489 --> 00:00:42.838
For fun, I also taught them how to use a lasso, and Jack took his everywhere.

8
00:00:42.839 --> 00:00:48.212
But all this work and play was wearing out their clothes.

9
00:00:48.213 --> 00:00:52.890
Therefore I decided to pay another visit to the wreck to replenish our wardrobes.

10
00:00:52.891 --> 00:00:57.442
I also wanted to see how much longer the vessel was likely to hold together.

11
00:00:57.443 --> 00:00:59.988
Luckily there hadn't been a storm yet.

12
00:00:59.989 --> 00:01:03.451
The three older boys and I set off in the sailboat.

13
00:01:03.452 --> 00:01:05.237
"Come, boys," I said.

14
00:01:05.238 --> 00:01:08.553
"Don't leave behind a single item of the slightest value.

15
00:01:08.554 --> 00:01:11.595
Search the ship to the bottom of its hold."

16
00:01:11.596 --> 00:01:13.994
The boys scattered throughout the ship.

17
00:01:13.995 --> 00:01:18.455
Soon everything from bales of cloth to window shutters lay in a heap on the deck.

18
00:01:18.456 --> 00:01:21.146
We loaded the sailboat and went onshore.

19
00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:24.914
After a few more trips, nothing remained.

20
00:01:24.915 --> 00:01:32.049
"I left two barrels of gunpowder on board and lit a very long fuse," I said to my wife when we returned to Tentholm.

21
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:36.036
That night we ate supper at a spot from which we could see the wreck.

22
00:01:36.037 --> 00:01:42.201
Suddenly a vivid pillar of fire rose from the black waters.

23
00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:48.464
"That's the end of the brave ship that carried us from Switzerland," I said softly.

24
00:01:48.465 --> 00:01:53.467
We had planned the destruction of the ship, but we went to bed that night feeling sad.

25
00:01:53.468 --> 00:01:56.597
We felt as if we'd lost a dear friend.

26
00:01:56.598 --> 00:02:00.730
The next morning we found the shore lined with a rich supply of wood.

27
00:02:00.731 --> 00:02:04.140
Our ship had been good to us until the end.

28
00:02:04.141 --> 00:02:09.803
Meanwhile Fritz and I had been planning another expedition into the countryside surrounding Falconhurst.

29
00:02:09.804 --> 00:02:13.546
"Why does Fritz always get to go?" complained Jack.

30
00:02:13.547 --> 00:02:20.280
"Yes," said my wife. "I'd like to see what's beyond Falconhurst too."

31
00:02:20.281 --> 00:02:25.318
So the next morning the whole family started off in our cart pulled by the cow and donkey.

32
00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:29.242
We took everything necessary for an expedition of several days.

33
00:02:29.243 --> 00:02:35.634
On the first day we gathered more berries to make candles and tapped the rubber trees for their gummy sap.

34
00:02:35.635 --> 00:02:41.494
After pitching our tent, we were enjoying supper when our donkey, Grizzle, let out a loud bray.

35
00:02:41.495 --> 00:02:46.196
"What's wrong with him?" asked little Franz as the donkey galloped away.

36
00:02:46.197 --> 00:02:51.745
"I have no idea," I replied, "but we can't afford to lose such a valuable animal."

37
00:02:51.746 --> 00:02:56.694
We followed the donkey for a short distance, but had to give up because it was getting dark.

38
00:02:56.695 --> 00:02:59.551
The next morning I took Jack and the dogs with me.

39
00:02:59.552 --> 00:03:04.894
We followed Grizzle's tracks in the soil until they mingled with those of other animals.

40
00:03:04.895 --> 00:03:11.507
At last we reached a wide plain, and I saw a herd of large animals. Buffalo!

41
00:03:11.508 --> 00:03:15.637
Turk and Juno saw them too and dashed forward before I could stop them.

42
00:03:15.638 --> 00:03:20.139
The dogs surrounded a young buffalo, causing the rest of the herd to attack.

43
00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:23.502
I fired my gun in the air, and the herd retreated.

44
00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:28.493
"If we could capture that little buffalo, we might train him to work for us," I said.

45
00:03:28.494 --> 00:03:31.098
"I know what to do!" said Jack.

46
00:03:31.099 --> 00:03:36.397
He pulled out his lasso and, twirling it in the air, caught the buffalo by the hind legs.

47
00:03:36.398 --> 00:03:39.150
We fastened a rope around the buffalo's neck.

48
00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:44.366
With the dogs herding it from either side, we managed to get the buffalo to walk with us.

49
00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:48.393
I decided to give up our donkey search for the moment and return to camp.

50
00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:52.158
Juno dashed ahead and was about to rush into a little cave.

51
00:03:52.159 --> 00:03:55.207
Suddenly a large jackal sprang out at her.

52
00:03:55.208 --> 00:04:00.382
Turk joined the fight, and the two dogs managed to drive off the jackal.

53
00:04:00.383 --> 00:04:02.724
Jack peered inside the cave.

54
00:04:02.725 --> 00:04:07.047
"Baby jackals! Oh, Father, may I take one home?"

55
00:04:07.048 --> 00:04:11.364
I glanced around nervously. "Hurry up before the parents come back."

56
00:04:11.365 --> 00:04:15.915
Jack went into the cave and emerged with a yellow cub the size of a cat.

57
00:04:15.916 --> 00:04:19.106
He was eager to show his new pet to his brothers.

58
00:04:19.107 --> 00:04:24.068
"Look what I found!" he said triumphantly when we arrived back at our tent.

59
00:04:24.069 --> 00:04:28.469
"And look what I found!" said Fritz, showing us a small eagle.

60
00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:32.337
"Now, boys," I said. "You're collecting a lot of pets.

61
00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:35.088
It's not your mother's job to take care of them.

62
00:04:35.089 --> 00:04:42.863
You must each look after your own, and if I find any animal neglected, I will set it free. Do you understand?"

63
00:04:42.864 --> 00:04:49.258
The boys nodded solemnly while my wife looked quite relieved.
